WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Berlin, 1743.

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.630
A young Jew from Dessau
arrives, following his teacher.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.090
Moses Mendelssohn teaches himself German,

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.160
Latin and philosophy.

5
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.870
In 1763 he wins the Berlin Academy prize,

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.270
ahead of Kant.

7
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.070
People call him the German Socrates.

8
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.460
And all his life, he
stays an observant Jew.

9
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:27.400
So can a Jew keep every commandment,
and still say reason alone can prove God

10
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.690
exists?

11
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.590
In this mission, you'll see how he argued
for God and for the soul without quoting

12
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.760
scripture.

13
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.600
Then you'll open his German Torah, and
meet the rabbis who objected to it.

14
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: find out if a Jew can keep
every commandment and still prove God

15
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.950
by reason alone.
